{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && git check-ignore cores/bench/implementation_notes.md || true && sed -n '1,160p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\ncores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n# Implementation notes: one-hot EX forwarding\n\n- Changed `forward_unit` to produce three mutually exclusive enables per\n  source: ID/EX value, EX/MEM result, and MEM/WB result. EX/MEM matches retain\n  priority over MEM/WB, and both destination comparisons continue to exclude\n  x0.\n- Replaced the encoded forwarding cases in `ex_stage` with masked operands\n  combined by OR. Updated the top-level select widths to match.\n- Added a guarded `core_pkg.sv` include in `core.sv`. The requested wildcard\n  Verilator lint command puts `core.sv` before `core_pkg.sv`; this makes that\n  command elaborate while the package guard preserves the regular package-first\n  build flow.\n- No tests or architecture files were changed.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Verilator lint: passed with the requested command.\n- Formal: passed, 53 passed and 0 failed, using\n  `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`.\n- Timing: Gowin place option 0 reported 192.036 ns / 150 cells on the\n  destination-register-to-data-address path (149 logic levels; Fmax 5.355 MHz).\n  The path still crosses forwarding and the ALU, but is shorter than the\n  hypothesis's stated baseline of 199.837 ns / 156 cells.\n- Cosim: passed for both ELF programs using `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n  The initial default-NRET invocation could not compile because the harness\n  expected channel 1, which this `nret: 1` core does not expose.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- One-hot masking preserves priority and passes formal and cosim, but the\n  timing report still identifies the forwarding-to-ALU address path as the\n  critical path. The measured Fmax may vary across placement options and runs.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
