{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git status --short && git diff --check && git diff --stat && sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv         | 25 ++++++++++++-----------\n cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv     |  2 ++\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv     | 18 ++++++++++++-----\n cores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv | 44 +++++++++++++++++++++++------------------\n cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv     |  7 +++++++\n cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv    |  7 ++++++-\n 6 files changed, 67 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added two 2-bit forwarding selectors to the ID/EX bundle. ID compares the\n  incoming IF/ID source tags with the current ID/EX and EX/MEM destination\n  tags, and captures the selections with the instruction.\n- Changed EX to use the registered selectors for EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypasses.\n  The ID/EX producer has priority over the EX/MEM producer because it is the\n  younger writer.\n- Added stage-qualified producer enables. EX and MEM determine whether a\n  producer will still write after alignment-trap handling, so a suppressed\n  younger write does not hide an older matching writer.\n- Kept the load-use hazard unit unchanged. Its one-cycle bubble gives the\n  dependent instruction a MEM/WB selection for a load in EX/MEM.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nThe forwarding decode also consumes effective write enables from EX and MEM\nto preserve trap behavior. The timing run's placement option 0 reports\n5.223 MHz and a critical path from a register-file entry through ID and the\nEX ALU to the data-memory output. The baseline experiment logged 5.442 MHz\nmedian, so this single-placement timing result does not establish a fitness\nimprovement; the register-file-to-ALU path is now the main concern.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Verilator lint: passed when `core_pkg.sv` was listed first. The literal\n  wildcard order lists `core.sv` before `core_pkg.sv` and fails before\n  elaboration because the compilation-unit typedefs are declared later.\n- Formal: passed, 53 checks, using automatic `nret: 1` wrapper/config\n  selection. An initial explicit `checks_si.cfg` invocation selected the\n  default dual-channel wrapper and failed at wrapper elaboration; rerunning\n  with auto-detection passed.\n- Cosim: passed for selftest and CoreMark with `NRET=1`. The default build\n  sets `NRET=2`, which does not match this core's declared single-channel\n  interface.\n- Gowin timing: placement option 0 reported 5.223 MHz, 147 logic levels,\n  12,245 LUT4s, 454 registers, 8 LUT-RAMs, 6 BSRAMs, and 6 DSPs.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
