{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r1s1.yaml && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-002-r1s1\ntitle: \"Predecode forwarding selections\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The baseline critical path starts at a MEM/WB destination register and crosses forwarding selection and the EX ALU before reaching the data-memory output. Register-destination equality checks are currently performed in EX, serializing compare, operand mux, and address arithmetic in one cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compute each incoming instruction's forwarding source while it is in ID, using the current ID/EX and EX/MEM producers, then register the two select codes alongside the ID/EX operands. In EX, use those registered selectors to choose the EX/MEM or MEM/WB bypass value. This moves register-tag comparisons off the forwarding-mux-to-ALU path while preserving the existing one-cycle load-use interlock and producer priority.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 12\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add registered source-selection fields to the ID/EX pipeline bundle.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Feed IF/ID source tags and ID/EX plus EX/MEM producer tags to early forwarding decode, capture its selections in ID, and route the registered selections to EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Decode next-cycle forwarding selections from IF/ID source registers and current ID/EX and EX/MEM destinations, with youngest-writer priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture the predecoded forwarding selections with each ID/EX instruction and hold or flush them with the rest of the stage.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
