{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md && rg -n 'structural|pipeline|stage|cache|single-cycle|fold|merge|register file|regfile' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-001-r1s0 (regression, +2.97%): Replacing EX forwarding muxes with three 32-bit one-hot AND/OR networks regressed, showing that replicated data gating can outweigh saved select decoding; check the mapped path before adopting this form.\n- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-003-r1s2 (improvement, +5.28%): A 16-entry 2-bit BHT indexed by branch PC can accelerate CoreMark's repeatedly taken loop branches by redirecting IF from the branch immediate and flushing only on EX prediction mismatch, without a target cache.\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"One-hot EX forwarding to shorten the critical path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline's worst path runs from the MEM/WB destination register through the forwarding unit and EX ALU to the memory address output, with 156 logic cells and 199.837 ns arrival time. The current two-bit priority select is decoded again by a three-way operand mux on this path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline's worst path runs from the MEM/WB destination register through the forwarding unit and EX ALU to the memory address output, with 156 logic cells and 199.837 ns arrival time. The current two-bit priority select is decoded again by a three-way operand mux on this path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the two-bit forwarding selects with mutually exclusive one-hot selects for the register-file value, EX/MEM result, and MEM/WB result. Apply these selects as bit masks and an OR in EX, allowing the FPGA LUT mapping to combine forwarding selection with the operand path and reduce the comparator-to-ALU delay while preserving EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate mutually exclusive one-hot forwarding enables per source operand, retaining the existing freshness priority and x0 exclusion.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace encoded case-based forwarding muxes with one-hot masked operand selection for bas\n…[8003 of 11075 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:501971b62e0fba59]…\n.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.76, \"delta_pct\": 5.28, \"vs_baseline\": 5.28, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.448, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4268786, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12935, \"ff\": 493, \"seeds\": [5.165, 5.448, 5.448], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.165, 144], [1, 5.448, 146], [2, 5.448, 146]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -188.601, \"arrival_ns\": 198.896, \"logic_cells\": 148, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 144, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T18:31:37.650679Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-003-r1s2 (improvement, +5.28%): A 16-entry 2-bit BHT indexed by branch PC can accelerate CoreMark's repeatedly taken loop branches by redirecting IF from the branch immediate and flushing only on EX prediction mismatch, without a target cache.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
