{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-002-r2s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Share an iterative divider outside the EX critical path\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The measured critical path runs through EX and the ALU before reaching the data-memory output. The ALU currently describes separate combinational signed and unsigned divide and remainder operators, which can dominate timing even though CoreMark exercises them much less often than ordinary ALU operations. Reusing one sequential divider trades occasional divide latency for a shorter common-cycle path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the four combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapaths with one 32-step restoring divider that handles signed and unsigned quotient and remainder requests. When a divide or remainder reaches EX, latch its forwarded operands and operation, let older pipeline work drain, then hold younger work and inject bubbles until the result is ready. Handle divide-by-zero and signed overflow explicitly, and retain the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS stand-ins for the formal build. Removing the large divide network from the ordinary EX combinational path should raise Fmax enough to offset the rare multicycle operations in CoreMark.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove the real combinational divide and remainder operators and select the iterative unit result for M-extension divide operations, preserving ALTOPS behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: \"Add one iterative restoring divider supporting DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU, including RV32M corner cases.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Start the divider from forwarded EX operands, retain the active operation, and complete its instruction only when the result is ready.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Interlock younger pipeline work during iterative division while preserving bus-stall, redirect, and retirement behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the multicycle EX interlock so older work drains once and a completed divide retires exactly once.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
