{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r1s2.yaml && cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Predict conditional branches with a small BHT\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Conditional branches currently resolve in EX, so every taken branch redirects fetch after wrong-path instructions have entered the pipeline. CoreMark contains tight loops where backward branches are commonly taken, making branch direction prediction a plausible way to improve iterations per cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a 16-entry table of 2-bit saturating direction counters indexed by the branch PC. In IF, predict conditional branches from the table and form a taken target directly from the fetched branch immediate. Carry the predicted next PC with the instruction, train the counter when the branch resolves in EX, and redirect/flush only on a mismatch. This should remove most taken-loop branch bubbles with modest state and without a target cache.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a small indexed table of saturating branch direction counters and update it from resolved conditional branches.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry the predicted next PC through the pipeline with the fetched instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Predict conditional branch direction during fetch and select the immediate target when taken.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Preserve the prediction metadata as the instruction enters ID/EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the resolved branch next PC with its prediction and request recovery only on a misprediction.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect predictor lookup, branch resolution feedback, and pipeline prediction metadata.\"\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
