{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'ls -l cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r2s2.yaml && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r2s2.yaml && git check-ignore -v cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r2s2.yaml || true'","aggregated_output":"-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench2 hwebench2 1754 Sep 29 20:34 cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r2s2.yaml\nid: hyp-20260929-003-r2s2\ntitle: \"Predict direct jumps and returns\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The existing BHT removes recovery bubbles for predictable conditional branches, but JAL and JALR still redirect from EX on every occurrence. JAL targets are encoded in the fetched instruction, and CoreMark's standard return instructions can reuse targets recorded from calls. Predicting these transfers in IF should remove recurring control-flow bubbles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Extend the existing fetch prediction to take direct JAL targets immediately and predict standard JALR returns from a small four-entry return address stack. Push the return PC for resolved JAL calls through x1 or x5, and pop on resolved JALR x0,0(x1/x5). Carry the predicted next PC with the instruction and compare it against EX resolution so only incorrect predictions redirect and flush; retain the current BHT path for conditional branches. This adds a focused predictor for unconditional control flow, which currently always pays EX redirect recovery.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry the predicted next PC through IF/ID and ID/EX to EX resolution.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Predict direct JAL targets and valid standard JALR return targets while preserving BHT branch prediction.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Preserve the fetch-stage predicted next PC in the ID/EX bundle.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare resolved next PC against the carried prediction for jumps as well as branches.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Add a small return address stack updated by resolved calls and returns, and connect prediction feedback.\"\n.gitignore:88:cores/*/experiments/hypotheses/\tcores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r2s2.yaml\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
